			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">Zophar the Naamathite answered and said:</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">because of my haste within me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">and out of my understanding a spirit answers me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">since man was placed on earth,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">and the joy of the godless but for a moment?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">and his head reach to the clouds,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">‘Where is he?’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">he will be chased away like a vision of the night.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">nor will his place any more behold him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">give back his wealth.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">down with him in the dust.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">under his tongue,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">and holds it in his mouth,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">cobras within him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">God casts them out of his belly.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">the tongue of a viper will kill him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">the streams flowing with honey and<crossref let="r" cid="c18020017.1" />curds.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">he will get no enjoyment.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">he has seized a house that he did not build.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">
				<crossref let="w" cid="c18020020.1" />he will not let anything in which he delights escape him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">therefore his prosperity will not endure.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">the hand of everyone in misery will come against him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">into his body.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">him through.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">terrors come upon him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">what is left in his tent will be consumed.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">and the earth will rise up against him.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">dragged off in the day of God's wrath.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">the heritage decreed for him by God.”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18020030">
